WEBVTT

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:05.120
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Officer and Central Judges of the Impeachment

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:05.460
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Court.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.510
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Sergeant at Arms is directed to make a proclamation.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:05:01.880
Senate Sergeant-at-Arms: All persons are commanded to keep silent under pain of penalty while the Impeachment Court is in session for the trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:10.620
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Impeachment Trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte is hereby called to order. We shall be led in prayer by Senator Judge Mark Villar.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:06:03.690
Sen. Mark A. Villar: Let us put ourselves in the presence of God. Almighty Father, we humbly stand before you today as we resume trial in this impeachment court. We beseech you to bless and inspire us so that all we think, say, and do aligns with your will. In times of adversity, we ask that you renew our spirit, keep our focus steady, and grant us the physical, emotional, and spiritual strength required for the magnitude of our responsibilities. We lean fully upon your grace to sustain us. Fill our hearts with wisdom, discernment, and integrity. Lighten our minds with clarity to carefully weigh the evidence before us, stripping away all confusions. We may examine every testimony and record the objective fairness, distinguishing truth from speculation. Shield us from the traps of personal bias, political variance, or divisiveness that could cloud our judgment, and grant us the grace to put the justice

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:07.970
Sen. Mark A. Villar: before gain, the plight of the Filipinos before our own, and truth above all.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:42.290
Sen. Mark A. Villar: Fill our hearts with wisdom and understanding in all our judgments that we may be effective channels of truth and justice. Grant us the grace of true independence, giving us courage to stand firm in what is right against political pressures and outside influences, remaining faithful to our solemn oath to the Constitution and the people we serve. Give us humility to seek your will, the truth that may be fully revealed under your light as we take our final steps. Continue to guide us so that peace and accountability may prevail. May our concluding judgment be rooted entirely in fairness, integrity, and righteousness for the fulfillment of your greater glory. In Jesus' name we pray. Amen.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:44.270
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Trial suspended.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:10.280
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Clerk of Court will now call the roll.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:24.440
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Roll call of members. The Honorable Senator Judge Aquino. Senator Judge Cayetano Alan. Senator Judge Cayetano Pia. Senator Judge Dela Rosa. Senator Judge Ejercito.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:15:03.340
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Senator Judge Estrada Senator Judge Go Senator Judge Hontiveros Senator Judge Lacson Senator Judge Lapid Senator Judge Legarda Senator Judge Marcoleta Senator Judge Marcos Senator Judge Padilla Senator Judge Pangilinan Senator Judge Sotto III Senator Judge Tulfo Erwin Senator Judge Tulfo Raffy Senator Judge Villanueva Senator Judge Villar Camille Senator Judge Villar Mark, Senator Judge Zubiri, the Presiding Officer Senator Judge Escudero, the Senate President Senator Judge Gatchalian.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:08.000
