07:12:34.620 --> 07:12:35.940
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: sinasala. Pag lumalabas

07:12:35.940 --> 07:12:37.920
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: na hindi auditable, hindi nyo na itutuloy.

07:12:37.980 --> 07:12:46.590
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Well, pag hindi siya auditable... Siyempre ayaw din po ng cliente yun na ipagawa sa amin kasi hindi naman po kami rubber stamp.

07:12:47.090 --> 07:12:47.570
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: So

07:12:47.570 --> 07:12:50.730
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: pagka hindi po siya auditable, magbabago po yung tulong namin.

07:12:50.970 --> 07:12:51.450
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Ang

07:12:51.450 --> 07:12:55.450
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: i-offer po namin, pwede ba kitang tulungan na i-improve ang books mo,

07:12:55.590 --> 07:12:56.010
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: mag

07:12:56.010 --> 07:13:12.590
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: -improve ang governance mo, mag-record ka ng maayos, mag-accounting ka ng maayos. So habang, pag natulungan po namin silang ganun, magiging auditable na po sila. Pero hindi po kami yung mag-audit. Kasi magkakaroon po kami ng independence issue na kami po lahat yung tumulong.

07:13:12.590 --> 07:13:13.250
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Tapos kayo rin

07:13:13.250 --> 07:13:13.850
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: na nag-audit.

07:13:13.850 --> 07:13:26.710
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Because that will be self-audit. Pero at least auditable na po sila. So lahat po yan, mangyayari po yan sa simula po, yung evaluation po. During the audit survey, pakikipag-usap po sa officers.

07:13:28.530 --> 07:13:35.550
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Titignan din po namin yung working papers po ng naon ng auditor. Ganun po yung mga prosesong gagawin.

07:13:35.550 --> 07:13:36.330
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So you have

07:13:38.530 --> 07:13:45.670
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Rarely, but you have issued adverse opinions. You have also issued qualified opinions.

07:13:45.670 --> 07:13:46.210
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Mas

07:13:46.210 --> 07:14:11.220
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: yung qualified opinion po ang, kasi yung qualified opinion po, maaari po siyang, based sa limbawa po sa accounting treatment. So yung accounting treatment, magkaiba po kami ng tingin. At gusto po ng clienteeng gawin yung kanila, yung sa amin naman iba yung tingin namin. Minsan po nagko-qualify po ng opinion on the effects po. Nung accounting po nila for a certain account. So

07:14:11.220 --> 07:14:25.600
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: dahil yung kanilang auditor ay nagbigay ng qualified opinion, so ano ang, to wrap this up, in layman's terms, ano ibig sabihin ng qualified opinion? Sa man on the street.

07:14:25.720 --> 07:14:41.560
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Ang qualified opinion po, ang sinasabi po niya, yung financial statements ayos sana eh. Kaso may konting problema sa gantong mga bagay. Yung sinasabi ko lamang po ay hindi po reliable yung financial statement.

07:14:41.800 --> 07:14:42.480
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Kung

07:14:42.480 --> 07:14:52.240
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: ang qualification mo cash at inventory at ang dahilan ng qualification mo ay hindi mo kasi tinignan o merong limitation, eh bakit ka nag clean opinion?

07:14:52.900 --> 07:14:53.580
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Hindi

07:14:53.580 --> 07:14:55.880
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: mo lang alam kung gaano kalaki yung...

07:14:57.630 --> 07:15:04.910
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Problema sa cash. Tulad po ng GenCorp po na sa computation namin merong 87% na under declaration.

07:15:05.370 --> 07:15:05.970
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: O

07:15:05.970 --> 07:15:10.330
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: hindi, baliwala na po yung qualified. Talagang adverse opinion dapat ang inabot po nun.

07:15:10.610 --> 07:15:13.850
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: At ang adverse opinion sa Tagalog?

07:15:13.930 --> 07:15:17.230
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Hindi mapagkakatiwalaan yung financial statement po.

07:15:17.530 --> 07:15:17.870
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay.

07:15:17.970 --> 07:15:20.230
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Salamat. Maraming salamat.

07:15:20.230 --> 07:15:20.830
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator

07:15:20.830 --> 07:15:22.170
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Judge Sotto is recognized.

07:15:27.200 --> 07:15:38.450
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Atty. Cabrera, my question would either elicit felicitations for you or not. But it's not directed to you. The question is to the presiding officer.

07:15:40.170 --> 07:15:49.190
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Mr. presiding officer, did Atty. Cabrera beat the record of Executive Director Benaventura?

07:15:50.810 --> 07:15:56.510
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Tinanong ko kayo kanina, Tito Sen, kung mahirap yung tanong sa sagot niyo. Buti na lang tinanong ko a few minutes ago.

07:15:57.090 --> 07:15:57.610
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: I

07:15:57.610 --> 07:15:58.150
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: will respond.

07:16:00.850 --> 07:16:17.840
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Depsek, Deputy Clerk of Court, Mavic just gave it to me. Labindalawang oras po umupo dyan si Atty. Ronel, si Atty. Cabrera, kumatapos tayo ng alasais, samput kalahating oras pa lang. So silver medalist lang ito kung saka

07:16:17.840 --> 07:16:18.160
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: -saka.

07:16:18.260 --> 07:16:31.200
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Okay, so you do not get my felicitations, but you receive my gratitude. Thank you very much for staying there, the witness. And that's all. Thank you, kind sir.

07:16:32.100 --> 07:16:33.980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Lacson is recognized.

07:16:35.350 --> 07:17:03.560
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: Two very quick points, Mr. President Officer, just so we can rectify and spread it to the records, about the SALN. With all due respect to the Presiding Officer, tama po si Artur Di Cabrera na pag-real estate, acquisition, pati improvements kasama. So, para lang maliwanag yung, this is a spare Section 8A of RA 6713.

07:17:05.580 --> 07:17:24.880
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: Pagka po personal properties, hindi kasama improvement. Alimbawa yung sports car ni Sen. Lapid, nilagyan ng mag-wheel. Hindi na po kailangan i-declare. So yun lang po. Pangalawa po, hindi ko alam kung fact-check ang tawag dito kasi chat GP ito yung aking reference.

07:17:26.890 --> 07:17:46.770
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: Yung isang franchise, isang store ng Jollibee, in 2022, 35 to 55. Tama po yun. Pero 2025, 40 million to 70, 45 million to 70 million. So tama po kayo. Very conservative yung inyong ginamit ng mga figures. Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

07:17:46.770 --> 07:17:47.010
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: And

07:17:47.010 --> 07:18:08.310
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: to continue with the SALN, while some forms include fair market value of the real property, it is not part of the computation of the net worth. Only acquisition cost is factored in with respect to computing the net worth as per civil service regulations. Just brief interjections from this representation before we call it a day.

07:18:12.890 --> 07:18:42.630
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Honorable Diokno, just to put everything in perspective, given that Atty. Cabrera is your last witness. Your Article 2 allegation in the complaint is Respondent VP Sarah Duterte committed culpable violation of the Constitution and betrayed public trust when she, quote, amassed unexplained wealth manifestly disproportionate to her lawful income and earnings during her incumbency as a public official. I presume this is for the period 2022 to 2025, correct?

07:18:42.630 --> 07:18:43.290
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your Honor.

07:18:43.290 --> 07:18:49.490
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: And that is why you presented bank officials, insurance officials, and the AMLC, I guess.

07:18:49.910 --> 07:18:50.530
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your Honor.

07:18:50.970 --> 07:19:11.150
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: B. Failed to fully and truthfully disclose all her and her spouse's assets, liabilities, net worth in her statement of assets and liabilities and net worth, including her SALN for 2022, 23, and 24. That is why, again, those witnesses were presented, including now, Attorney Cabrera.

07:19:11.350 --> 07:19:12.050
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your Honor.

07:19:12.980 --> 07:19:25.580
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: failed to divest and instead willfully continued all her business interests during her tenure as VP for the years 22 to 2025. That's why the SEC was presented, I guess.

07:19:25.980 --> 07:19:28.120
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: As well as the SALNs, if your honor, please.

07:19:28.320 --> 07:19:36.660
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: As well as the SALNs with the Office of the Ombudsman, yes, correct. Thank you, Honorable Diokno. No, still on you.

07:19:38.350 --> 07:19:43.730
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, you alleged unexplained wealth, correct?

07:19:44.360 --> 07:19:45.060
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your Honor.

07:19:45.340 --> 07:19:47.760
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Which is different from ill-gotten wealth.

07:19:48.120 --> 07:19:48.920
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your Honor.

07:19:49.200 --> 07:19:55.770
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ika nga sa Tagalog, unexplained wealth, hindi may paliwanag na yaman, ill-gotten wealth, nakaw na yaman.

07:19:55.770 --> 07:19:56.750
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your Honor.

07:19:56.750 --> 07:20:01.370
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hidden wealth also you did not allege. Sa Tagalog, tagong yaman.

07:20:01.370 --> 07:20:02.450
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your Honor.

07:20:02.450 --> 07:20:10.340
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Now, what Atty. Cabrera, Atty. Alex stated is unexplained wealth, which is not exactly defined by law.

07:20:12.350 --> 07:20:15.810
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Or are you aware of any law that defines unexplained wealth?

07:20:16.190 --> 07:20:20.370
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I believe it appears in Section 8 of Republic Act 1319. In

07:20:20.370 --> 07:20:22.790
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: connection with the declaration that you have to make?

07:20:22.790 --> 07:20:23.310
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes,

07:20:23.430 --> 07:20:27.030
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: in connection with Republic Act 1379, Section 2, Your Honor.

07:20:27.470 --> 07:20:31.550
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Again, in relation to the declarations you have to make?

07:20:31.550 --> 07:20:32.070
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes.

07:20:32.270 --> 07:20:32.530
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Correct?

07:20:32.890 --> 07:20:33.650
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your Honor.

07:20:33.830 --> 07:20:35.850
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, thank you very much, Honorable Diokno.

07:20:36.250 --> 07:20:37.110
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Attorney Alex,

07:20:38.410 --> 07:20:42.370
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You know the definition of unexplained wealth when you used it in your tables?

07:20:43.470 --> 07:20:43.990
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Apo.

07:20:45.510 --> 07:20:55.010
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Unexplained wealth po is the property, the value of the property acquired which is manifestly disproportionate po to the income. Yun po yung ginamit ko po.

07:20:55.830 --> 07:21:12.880
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Now, you pierced the corporate veil. Para sa simpleng salita, isinangtabi nyo yung pagkakaroon ng hiwalay na personalidad ng isang korporasyon sangayon sa batas at tinignan nyo. Yung aktual na mga may-ari sa likod ng korporasyon na iyon, yung mga stockholders mismo, tama po ba?

07:21:13.320 --> 07:21:13.920
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Tama po.

07:21:14.340 --> 07:21:28.540
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Under existing law, as a lawyer too and as an accountant, you can only do that for three reasons. Number one, kapag ka ginamit po yung korporasyon para makaiwas sa mga bayarin o mga kontraktual na obligasyon, ito po ba yun o

07:21:28.540 --> 07:21:29.220
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: hindi?

07:21:29.220 --> 07:21:29.740
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Hindi po.

07:21:30.580 --> 07:21:35.980
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Kasama kung yung kontraktual po, hindi po namin alam kung sino po yung pinagkakaupang.

07:21:35.980 --> 07:21:50.040
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hindi nga po yun yung base yan. So hindi po. Ang pangalawa, fraud, illegality or perpetration of a wrong. The corporation is used to justify a wrong, protect fraud, commit or conceal a crime, circumvent a statute or work injustice against another.

07:21:50.860 --> 07:21:54.860
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Pwede na po magamit po yung pangalawa pong yan dahil po sa tax fraud po.

07:21:55.580 --> 07:22:08.180
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Pangatlo, alter ego or instrumentality. The corporation is a mere farce, business conduit, adjunct or instrumentality. with no genuinely separate mind, will, or existence in the transactions involved.

07:22:09.230 --> 07:22:13.570
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Yan po, possibility po yung pangatlo pero yung pangalawa po yung ginamit po namin.

07:22:13.790 --> 07:22:16.250
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Pero ang nasa ilalim po nung pangalawa ay fraud.

07:22:16.750 --> 07:22:17.330
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Fraud po.

07:22:17.690 --> 07:22:23.550
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So ang rason nyo kung bakit nyo isinantabi yung separate corporate personality ay fraud?

07:22:24.610 --> 07:22:25.330
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Tama po.

07:22:27.170 --> 07:22:49.280
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Nakita ko po yung ginawa ninyo sa GenCorp, unahin po natin yan. Binanggit na rin ito kanina nila Sen. Pia at Sen. Camille. Kung tama ang sinabi sa valuation base sa open source ni Senator Judge Lacson ng halaga ng Jollibee conservatively at 35 million, nilagay niyo po sa page 10 ang inyong findings. You can check your findings, sir. Yung 35 million.

07:22:49.660 --> 07:22:50.360
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Tama po.

07:22:50.540 --> 07:22:58.080
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Nilagay niyo po, kada taon nag-contribute yung shareholder na si VP Sara ng 35 million. Tama po ba? Ay hindi

07:22:58.080 --> 07:22:58.440
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: po.

07:22:58.440 --> 07:22:58.720
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ano

07:22:58.720 --> 07:22:58.800
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: po?

07:22:59.040 --> 07:23:06.520
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Yung 35 million po doon, yung po yung... continuously undeclared na attributed capital po namin.

07:23:08.520 --> 07:23:12.020
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Attributed na capital contribution nino? Ni

07:23:12.020 --> 07:23:18.460
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: BP Sara po. Yung 35 po, nauulit lang po yun dahil it continues to be undeclared po.

07:23:18.840 --> 07:23:23.900
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So hindi to, so minsan lang to dahil kung limang Jollibee branches times 5 is 175.

07:23:24.380 --> 07:23:24.900
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Tama po.

07:23:24.920 --> 07:23:25.140
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hindi po ba?

07:23:25.240 --> 07:23:25.800
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Tama po.

07:23:25.800 --> 07:23:27.800
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So dahil 20% divided by 5, 35.

07:23:28.200 --> 07:23:28.660
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Tama po.

07:23:28.760 --> 07:23:35.040
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So hindi po ito na double booking, binanggit lang na... Kada taon, ito yung halagang hindi na dedeklara.

07:23:35.220 --> 07:23:35.580
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Pero

07:23:35.580 --> 07:23:38.520
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: hindi ito kinarga ng limang beses doon sa 817.

07:23:39.400 --> 07:23:40.000
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Tama po?

07:23:40.000 --> 07:23:40.880
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Tama po.

07:23:41.080 --> 07:24:00.580
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ngayon, pagdating naman po sa Metro Chow, sinabi niyo po, advance from shareholders. Pareho din po ng GenCorp, dahil wala naman pong capital contribution na diretso yung mga shareholders sa authorized capital stock, in-assume po natin, base sa AFS, na nag-advance yung mga shareholders. Tama po?

07:24:01.360 --> 07:24:04.920
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Yung sa AFS po yung may advances lang po is Cale88 po.

07:24:04.960 --> 07:24:08.380
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ah, Cale88 lang. Eto pong GenCorp, in-assume lang po ninyo ito.

07:24:08.820 --> 07:24:10.120
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Ay, nasa GIS po yan.

07:24:11.080 --> 07:24:13.220
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yung shares po, hindi yung advances of shareholders.

07:24:13.680 --> 07:24:17.300
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Ay, wala po kaming advances ng GenCorp.

07:24:17.300 --> 07:24:20.780
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: There is no record of advances of shareholders for GenCorp. Wala

07:24:20.780 --> 07:24:23.720
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: po. GenCorp and Metro City Chow po wala po.

07:24:23.720 --> 07:24:26.380
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Wala po. So Cale lang ang may advances of shareholders.

07:24:26.820 --> 07:24:27.140
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Tama po.

07:24:27.180 --> 07:24:32.290
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So pag sinabi mo pong advances ng shareholders, pautang po ito? shareholder sa kumpanya.

07:24:32.910 --> 07:24:36.410
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Pautang po ng shareholder sa kumpanya po. So,

07:24:36.490 --> 07:24:38.750
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: binook niyo po ito as asset receivable.

07:24:41.270 --> 07:24:42.530
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Tama po, receivable.

07:24:43.270 --> 07:24:45.960
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Pautang eh. Sa kumpanya po.

07:24:46.320 --> 07:24:48.560
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Sa kumpanya? Sige, sila po

07:24:48.560 --> 07:24:49.880
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: dapat, sila po dapat yun.

07:24:49.880 --> 07:24:51.400
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Payable po yan ng kumpanya po.

07:24:51.940 --> 07:24:54.500
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Utang nga po ng kumpanya kay vice president.

07:24:54.880 --> 07:24:58.350
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Ah, sa... kay Atty. Manz Carpio. Ah,

07:24:58.410 --> 07:25:00.270
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: sorry, sorry, kay Atty. Manz, yung Cali. So,

07:25:00.290 --> 07:25:02.830
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: payable po yan ng Cali88.

07:25:03.070 --> 07:25:05.650
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Utang po ng Cali88 yan kay Atty. Manz.

07:25:05.770 --> 07:25:06.230
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Tama po.

07:25:06.650 --> 07:25:09.870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hindi pa po nababayaran. So, receivable po siya.

07:25:11.010 --> 07:25:14.730
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Receivable po siya ni Atty. Manz po. Payable po siya ng company po.

07:25:15.230 --> 07:25:19.430
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Payable ng company, receivable ni Atty. Manz. Matuturin niyo po bang asset yan?

07:25:19.850 --> 07:25:20.250
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Na

07:25:20.250 --> 07:25:21.870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: kailangan ideklara sa SALN?

07:25:22.070 --> 07:25:22.810
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Dapat rin po.

07:25:23.310 --> 07:25:24.870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Bakit po? Hindi pa naman bayad yung utang.

07:25:25.640 --> 07:25:29.960
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Hindi po. Dapat po siyang i-deklara po sa SALN po.

07:25:31.370 --> 07:25:32.190
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Bakit nga po?

07:25:32.490 --> 07:25:33.990
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Dahil po receivable po siya.

07:25:34.550 --> 07:25:44.670
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So lahat ng receivables from the accounting point of view, maski hindi pa aktual na nababayaran, kailangan mo i-deklara bilang parte ng asset mo.

07:25:44.910 --> 07:25:45.390
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Tama po.

07:25:46.120 --> 07:26:04.560
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kasi baliktad po, kapag nag-advance naman ako sa future dividends, utang ko naman yun. Bale yun eh. Parang bumalay ako sa kumpanya. Bumalay ako sa boss ko. Yun naman po ay utang ng shareholder sa kumpanya. Di

07:26:04.560 --> 07:26:04.980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: ba?

07:26:04.980 --> 07:26:07.540
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Apo, advances to employees po.

07:26:07.540 --> 07:26:07.980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kahit

07:26:07.980 --> 07:26:08.420
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: shareholder.

07:26:08.780 --> 07:26:09.360
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Or stockholders.

07:26:10.060 --> 07:26:10.500
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You

07:26:10.730 --> 07:26:15.250
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: mentioned the amounts of money that came in and out of the corporations.

07:26:15.890 --> 07:26:16.330
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: And

07:26:16.330 --> 07:26:20.930
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: sabi mo, pumasok yan dyan, alang nga namang hindi nila pinaghati yan. Di ba yun po

07:26:20.930 --> 07:26:21.310
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: yung sabi niyo?

07:26:21.470 --> 07:26:25.280
Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera: Pag hindi po pumasok, Pag hindi po pumasok.

07:26:25.380 --> 07:26:30.880
