07:43:50.880 --> 07:43:53.080
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: That is noted. Attorney Sheila, you may proceed.

07:43:53.400 --> 07:45:12.530
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: Yes, Your Honor. We've heard over the last four or five hours of interpolations and interjections from the members, honorable members of this court, the term piercing of the corporate veil. We have here Kukan International Corporation versus Reyes, and I believe this is a matter of mandatory judicial notice for this court, where the court said, to disregard the separate juridical personality of a corporation, the wrongdoing must be established clearly and convincingly. cannot be presumed. Otherwise, an injustice that was never unintended may result from an erroneous application. And it bears reiterating that piercing the veil of corporate fiction is frowned upon. And these are the words of the Supreme Court in Kukan International Corporation v. Reyes so that we don't mislead the public na nanonood sa atin. Tutal, naglaan tayo ng napakahabang panahon at oras para pag-usapan ng mga korporasyon na ito ang opinion ng witness na binigyan ng mahigit limang oras para magbigay ng kanyang mga konklusyon at ng kanyang mga opinion.

07:45:14.750 --> 07:46:19.820
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: Mas maganda na maunawaan at malaman ng ating mga kababayan kung ano ba ang sabi ng Korte Suprema dito. Ito ang sabi ng Korte Suprema. "It cannot be presumed. To disregard the separate juridical personality of a corporation, the wrongdoing must be established clearly and convincingly." Again. "It cannot be presumed." Now, that witness has answered over time and repeatedly that, unang-una sa lahat, wala siyang sapat na oras. Pangalawa, hindi niya hawak ang lahat ng dokumento to form sufficient basis or ng kompletong opinion. Kaya hindi ko alam kung saan nanggaling ang kanyang mga opinion na ipinalaganap niya buong maghapon sa bulwagang ito at sa harap ng sambayang Pilipino. Anyway, your honor, that's my first manifestation. Of course, I presume that the prosecution has a comment to my manifestation.

07:46:19.820 --> 07:46:20.140
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes,

07:46:20.140 --> 07:46:21.960
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: if I may be heard, if your honor, please.

07:46:22.300 --> 07:46:22.320
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I

07:46:22.320 --> 07:46:24.200
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: was hoping otherwise, but I doubt that.

07:46:24.480 --> 07:46:25.000
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sorry,

07:46:25.040 --> 07:46:25.160
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: your honor.

07:46:25.160 --> 07:46:25.460
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Honorable

07:46:25.460 --> 07:46:26.520
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Diokno is recognized.

07:46:27.060 --> 07:48:04.880
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I believe these statements by the defense counsel are really out of place. That's meant for a closing argument, perhaps, but not for this time. before this court. And again, if I may bring to the attention of the court other Supreme Court decisions which I believe hold otherwise compared to what the good counsel has been trying to push before this honorable court. Rodrigo Villanueva v. People, GR No. 218652, Feb. 23, 2022. Piercing of corporate veil is allowed if juridical entities are used as vehicles. to commit illegal acts. I quote, Since accused Villanueva used said companies as means or vehicles for the circumvention of statutes, in this case governing procurement of government supplies, etc., such acts should not be countenanced and the court pierced the corporate veil. You have another case, Concept Builders v. NLRC, GR No. 108-734, 29 May 1996. Again, to the same effect. And there's another case, if your honor please, Toledo Construction Corporation Employees Association versus Toledo Construction Corporation where the court said that although mere ownership by a single stockholder or by another corporation is not of itself sufficient ground for disregarding the separate corporate personality, this can be disregarded if it is shown that the corporation is used in a fraudulent scheme.

07:48:06.570 --> 07:49:39.760
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: Your Honor, I think I need to respond to that manifestation just so we do not mislead the public again with respect to these points of law, Your Honor. I think with the points or the portions of the decisions stated by or mentioned by the gentleman in response to what I had stated earlier are actually Not inconsistent with the principle of law that I had stated earlier. Again, I will repeat. To disregard the separate juridical personality of a corporation, the wrongdoing must be established clearly and convincingly. It cannot be presumed. Now, the first case that was recited by the gentleman stated that since the accused committed etc. etc. actually supports The decision that I just cited. It means that if there was already a finding by the court that the accused had indeed committed certain things then the same had already gone through trial which also supports that the presumption had been or that the wrongdoing cannot be presumed your honor and therefore must be proved. And the second and third cases that he had cited which according to him also are of the same point, actually are not inconsistent with this principle, Your Honor. It cannot

07:49:39.760 --> 07:49:41.040
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: be presumed. The

07:49:41.040 --> 07:49:46.100
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: wrongdoing cannot be presumed. It has to be clearly and convincingly established.

07:49:47.220 --> 07:49:48.680
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Just one sentence.

07:49:50.600 --> 07:49:55.260
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Let's finish this, Honorable Diokno, with your indulgence. The court instructed,

07:49:56.080 --> 07:50:43.800
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The presiding officers instructed the clerk of court to take note of the cases cited by both parties. We shall reproduce the same and furnish all the senator judges through their official emails with a copy of the three cases mentioned by the Honorable Diokno and the case cited by Attorney Sheila for their information and reference. As you stated, as Attorney Sheila stated, This is a decision of the court and the court can take judicial notice of it since any arguments, further arguments from the counsels on this matter. Let the senator judges evaluate them on its face and based on their reading and appreciation of the actual cases cited by both parties. Move on to your next manifestation, Atty. Sheila, please.

07:50:43.840 --> 07:50:48.660
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Your Honor, before we get to the second manifestation, may I just make a brief statement? I think it should be clear in the record.

07:50:48.660 --> 07:50:49.980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You said one sentence, okay.

07:50:49.980 --> 07:50:50.460
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your

07:50:50.460 --> 07:51:21.600
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Honor. Insofar as clear and convincing evidence is concerned, assuming that good counsel is correct, ano pa po ba ang clear and convincing kundi yung naipakita natin kanina that 69% of one of the companies was undeclared and unreported income and 51% of the other company, Metro City Crown, was also undeclared and unreported. So, what kind of clear and convincing evidence do we need if that is not yet clear and convincing in itself?

07:51:21.960 --> 07:51:25.220
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: Oh, forgive me, Your Honor. I thought the gentleman had actually...

07:51:25.220 --> 07:51:25.880
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: That's exactly my

07:51:25.880 --> 07:51:31.240
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: problem, Honorable Diokno. This will not stop. Atty. Sheila, let that be the last statement on this matter.

07:51:31.240 --> 07:51:45.400
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: I'm sorry, Your Honor, but this involves the right of the respondent because, forgive me, I just heard just a few minutes ago that the gentleman said that this is not yet the time for any closing statement, Your Honor. And he

07:51:45.400 --> 07:51:46.000
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: may

07:51:46.000 --> 07:51:56.300
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: have forgotten that the respondent has not yet even began presenting its evidence, Your Honor. So, to conclude or to make that conclusion, that's out of order.

07:51:57.420 --> 07:52:19.240
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Well, to be fair, let that remain in the record too. And he was given a better opportunity earlier actually through an interjection of a senator judge which he did not take advantage of. Let that remain in the record as well for whatever it's worth. Again, let that be the last statement on this matter on piercing the corporate veil. Your next manifestation, attorney Sheila.

07:52:19.240 --> 07:52:19.520
