07:52:19.540 --> 07:53:31.300
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: your honor. Again, good afternoon. I heard the presiding officer mentioned earlier that there will still be a setting tomorrow for some administrative matters. However, it's only 547 and it has been repeated over and over again by the prosecution that they would want to streamline the proceeding and achieve speed. In this case, we're here, the prosecution. Both the prosecution and the respondent are here and I think the only remaining administrative matter on the part of the prosecution without of course encroaching in their prerogative is that since they had already Withdraw Article 3 and had manifested yesterday that this witness is already their last witness, then the next would be the formal offer which I think this court can settle today and give the parties time to file their respective pleadings thereon so that we also save time and both the prosecution and the respondent would no longer be required to return here for administrative matters.

07:53:31.300 --> 07:54:22.890
